# Russia: the non-working public holidays of the Russian Federation, the days off and working Saturdays the
# government moves around them every year, and the key-rate meetings of the Bank of Russia.
#
# Translated from holidays-events rules/catalog/ru_cis.yaml.
#
# Background (from the catalog file): Russia's non-working holidays are listed in article 112 of the Labour Code. When
# a holiday falls on a Saturday or Sunday, the law moves the day off to the next working day, but the government
# regularly redirects such days off by decree to other dates, often to build longer breaks (for 2025 the days off
# owed for 23 February and 8 March, both on a weekend, were moved to 8 May and 13 June; 24 February and 10 March stayed
# working days). The rules below therefore give only the holiday itself, on its calendar date. The transferred days
# off and the make-up working Saturdays are not projected: they are taken from the government decree, which the Bank
# of Russia lists on its holidays page, usually published in the autumn of the year before.
#
# How to read a rule: "rule <key> for <event> in <scope> = <dates> with kind = ..., cites ...;" says on which days the
# event <event> happens for the country or institution <scope>. "7 JAN" is 7 January of every year; "[1 JAN : 8 JAN]"
# is every day from 1 to 8 January inclusive; "3 FRI DEC" is the third Friday of December; "16 MAR > NEXT FRI" is the
# first Friday strictly after 16 March, i.e. the Friday on or after 17 March; "> PRECEDING ON country:RU" moves a date
# that is not a Russian business day to the business day before. "ANNOUNCED BY <source> [ELSE <dates>]" means the
# authority publishes the dates itself and those published dates always win; the expression after ELSE only gives
# projected dates for the years not yet published (without ELSE there are no dates until the announcement). The kind
# says what the day does: "closed" (a non-working day), "working_day" (a weekend day that is worked), "event" (a dated
# event such as a rate decision; the day stays a normal business day). "cites" names the source; "label official"
# means that source is the authority itself. The full syntax is in README.md in this directory. Weekends are declared
# in weekends.rules (both scopes here have the Saturday-Sunday weekend).
#
# Scopes used in this file:
#   country:RU         Russia (Russian Federation), a country; time zone Europe/Moscow.
#   central_bank:CBR   Bank of Russia (Central Bank of the Russian Federation), the central bank of Russia; its Board
#                      of Directors sets the key rate. Time zone Europe/Moscow; it follows Russia's business days.


# ===================================================================================================================
# Russia (country:RU)
# ===================================================================================================================

# New Year holidays: 1 to 8 January, all eight days are non-working days. Labour Code article 112 (as amended in
# 2012, in force since 2013) makes 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 8 January the New Year holidays; 7 January in between is
# Orthodox Christmas (its own rule below), so the whole block 1-8 January is off. Set by federal law (the Labour Code);
# the Bank of Russia lists the days each year. The rule applies from 1 January 2013. If some of these days fall on a
# weekend, the government usually moves the owed days off elsewhere by decree; those moved days are the separate
# rule ru.transferred_day_off.
rule ru.new_year_holidays for ru_new_year_holidays in country:RU valid from 2013-01-01
  = [1 JAN : 8 JAN]
  with kind = closed, note "1-6 and 8 January; 7 January is Orthodox Christmas"
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Orthodox Christmas, 7 January (Christmas by the Julian calendar of the Russian Orthodox Church, which falls on
# 7 January of the Gregorian calendar). A non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112. Always on its date; a
# day off owed for a weekend occurrence is a government transfer (ru.transferred_day_off).
rule ru.orthodox_christmas for orthodox_christmas in country:RU
  = 7 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Defender of the Fatherland Day, 23 February. Non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112. Only the date
# itself is given; if it falls on a weekend the substitute day off is set by government decree (see
# ru.transferred_day_off), and it is not always the next Monday (in 2025 it was moved to 8 May).
rule ru.defender_day for defender_of_the_fatherland_day in country:RU
  = 23 FEB
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# International Women's Day, 8 March. Non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112. Only the date itself; a
# substitute day off for a weekend occurrence is set by government decree (in 2025 it was moved to 13 June).
rule ru.womens_day for international_womens_day in country:RU
  = 8 MAR
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Spring and Labour Day, 1 May. Non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112. Only the date itself; substitute
# days off are set by government decree.
rule ru.spring_labour_day for labour_day in country:RU
  = 1 MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Victory Day, 9 May (end of the Second World War in Europe, by Moscow time). Non-working holiday under Labour Code
# article 112. Only the date itself; substitute days off are set by government decree.
rule ru.victory_day for victory_day in country:RU
  = 9 MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Russia Day, 12 June (the national day). Non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112. Only the date itself;
# substitute days off are set by government decree.
rule ru.russia_day for russia_day in country:RU
  = 12 JUN
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Unity Day (National Unity Day), 4 November. Non-working holiday under Labour Code article 112, introduced in 2005
# (the rule applies from 1 January 2005). Only the date itself; substitute days off are set by government decree.
rule ru.unity_day for unity_day in country:RU valid from 2005-01-01
  = 4 NOV
  with kind = closed
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Transferred day off (a "bridge"): a working day that the Russian government turns into a day off, either because a
# holiday fell on a weekend or to join a holiday to a weekend. The days are fixed each year by a government decree,
# usually published in September or October of the previous year, and listed by the Bank of Russia on its holidays
# page. They follow no rule (the government picks them freely), so no dates are projected: the rule has dates only
# once the decree is announced.
rule ru.transferred_day_off for transferred_day_off in country:RU
  = ANNOUNCED BY cbr_holidays
  with kind = closed, note "Government decree, usually September-October of the previous year"
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;

# Make-up working day: a Saturday (or other weekend day) that the government declares a working day, usually in
# exchange for a transferred day off elsewhere. Fixed by the same yearly government decree (usually published in
# September or October of the previous year) and listed by the Bank of Russia. Not projected; dates only once
# announced. Kind working_day: the weekend day becomes a business day.
rule ru.makeup_workday for makeup_workday in country:RU
  = ANNOUNCED BY cbr_holidays
  with kind = working_day, note "Government decree, usually September-October of the previous year"
  cites "Bank of Russia list of non-working holidays and transferred days off" url "https://www.cbr.ru/other/holidays/" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Bank of Russia (central_bank:CBR)
# ===================================================================================================================

# Bank of Russia key rate decision: the Board of Directors' meeting on the key rate (the policy interest rate). The
# Bank of Russia publishes its meeting calendar for the coming year (source cbr_key_rate_calendar; it holds eight
# regular meetings a year, always on Fridays, plus occasional extraordinary ones); the press release comes at 13:30
# and the press conference at 15:00 Moscow time. The published dates always win (for example 2027: 12 February,
# 19 March, 30 April, 11 June, 30 July, 10 September, 22 October, 17 December).
# For years not yet published, four of the eight meetings are projected from an observed pattern (not a Bank of Russia
# statement), checked against its own dates 2016-2027:
#   - the Friday on or after 17 March (11 of 12 years),
#   - the Friday on or after 24 April (11 of 12 years),
#   - the fourth Friday of October (12 of 12),
#   - the third Friday of December (12 of 12);
# for the October and December meetings, if that Friday is not a Russian business day, the business day before is
# taken. The other four meetings (February, June, July, September) move too much and are not projected. A meeting does
# not close any market; the session gives the window from the press release to the press conference.
rule cbr.key_rate_decision for cbr_key_rate_decision in central_bank:CBR
  = ANNOUNCED BY cbr_key_rate_calendar
    ELSE 16 MAR > NEXT FRI, 23 APR > NEXT FRI,
         4 FRI OCT > PRECEDING ON country:RU, 3 FRI DEC > PRECEDING ON country:RU
  with kind = event, session 13:30 - 15:00 tz "Europe/Moscow",
       note "Eight regular meetings a year; only March, April, October and December are projected"
  cites "Bank of Russia key rate meeting calendar" url "https://www.cbr.ru/eng/dkp/cal_mp/" label official;
